## Phase 9 — Global Illumination Cleanup

**Goal:** Keep GI optional and visually meaningful without exposing algorithm internals.

- Debug exposes Enabled, Quality and Strength only.
- Quality presets own rays/probe budgets/probe dimensions/bounce budgets/photon limits internally.
- Photon mapping remains an implementation choice rather than a player-facing toggle unless a later visual mode genuinely requires it.
- A baked/static-probe path is not added merely because it is conventional; it must be justified by representative GAME-scene measurements.

Current acceleration/profiling state:
- GI profiling hooks live in `GlobalIllumination::Debug` and report CPU scene-sync, update classification, photon rebuild and probe-update cost. These are CPU timings and are never presented as GPU timings.
- Rigid world geometry uses reusable 8-triangle-leaf mesh BLAS data plus an instance TLAS.
- Skinned/deformed geometry remains on the legacy world-space fallback.
- GI and Volumetrics share one CPU acceleration state.
- Volumetrics uploads the same flat TLAS/BLAS representation to SDL_GPU.
- Closest-hit traversal is near-child-first; occlusion uses a dedicated any-hit path.
- Synthetic scaling confirms one BLAS is reused across 1/16/64/256 instances while probe solve cost remains negligible.
- Before transform-refit optimization, 256 shared-BLAS instances measured 3.216 ms median transform/TLAS sync; transform-only TLAS updates are now implemented as stable-topology AABB refits and require a post-change benchmark rerun.

