## Phase 11 — Lightweight Render Graph

**Goal:** Keep pass/resource ownership clean as the rasterizer grows.

`Renderer::RenderGraph::Graph` is intentionally small. It owns logical resource read/write dependencies, explicit pass dependencies, stable topological scheduling, cycle/multi-writer validation, transient logical lifetime ranges and pass callbacks. It does not wrap SDL_GPU resources or command recording.

The Rasterizer currently uses the graph for the dependency-sensitive pre-opaque chain:

```text
Depth
 ├── Hi-Z
 │    └── Visibility
 │         └── GPU Draw Compaction
 └── AO

Lighting
 └── Forward+
```

Shadow updates remain explicit because they own independent dirty-layer caching. Sky/PBR/camera-layer render-pass command recording also remains direct SDL_GPU code rather than being hidden behind a giant graph abstraction.

